# Built corpus output is committed on purpose (ADR-001): its diff is the review surface for
# a mapping change, the way a golden file is the review surface for a snapshot test.
# Marking it generated collapses that diff by default in GitHub's PR view and labels it, so
# the output does not drown the mapping change that produced it. It stays one click away.
#
# Conflict policy: a conflict under dist/ is resolved by REBUILDING, never by hand-merging.
# A hand-merged output is a file no build produces, which is the one thing this repo claims
# cannot happen.
sources/*/dist/** linguist-generated=true

# Verbatim third-party input. Never normalized, never touched by an eol filter.
sources/*/input/** -text
